  "published": "2026-04-25T03:24:37.56Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.1.7 stable: Version-sync with SpawnDev.WebTorrent 3.1.7. No source changes in WebTorrent.Server itself. WebTorrent 3.1.7 adds a new `TcpListenerService` for inbound BT peer connections (closes the seed-C# / leech-mainline audit gap) and ships two wire-level correctness fixes that benefit every consumer seeding to a pipelining leecher: `Wire._message` now sends header + data in a single buffer (was two separate writes that could interleave bytes between concurrent `SendPiece` responses, corrupting the wire and tripping mainline-client hash verification), and `TcpPeer.AttachAsync` is split from `StartReadLoop` to avoid a kernel-buffered-handshake drop race. See SpawnDev.WebTorrent 3.1.7 release notes for the full write-up.",
